    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12771" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-gĕro</span></b> ,
		ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to carry away, carry off</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de vinea sarmenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato R.
					R. 37, 5</span></i>
			 Schneid. <i>N. cr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mea ornamenta ad meretrices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. 5, 2, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurum meum tuae amicae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 1, 41</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">Plin. 12, 27, 60, § 131</span></i>, the
			true reading is digeritur).</div>
